Package: nonprobsvyMC
Type: Package
Title: Misclassification-Corrected Mass Imputation for Non-Probability Samples
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Maciej", "Beresewicz", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "maciej.beresewicz@ue.poznan.pl",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8281-4301")))
Description: Bridges the 'nonprobsvy' inference framework for non-probability
    samples with the misclassification-corrected generalized linear models of
    'mismeasured'. Provides 'nonprob_mc()', a mass-imputation estimator of the
    population mean whose outcome model corrects for a misclassified discrete
    covariate declared with the 'mc()' formula term (naive, additive and
    multiplicative bias corrections, and the corrected-score estimator).
    Returns 'nonprob'-class objects, so the 'nonprobsvy' methods (print,
    summary, confint, nobs, weights, pop_size) work unchanged. The variance
    combines the design-based component from the 'survey' package with the
    corrected-score linearization of the outcome-model uncertainty.
